H1107:
only definitions are written at the top level of {file, select, testfile {a test file} other {a module}}; this statement does not run {file, select, testfile {outside the tests} other {when the module is imported}} (1.1): move it into a function and call setup() {file, select, testfile {in the test that needs it} other {in the importing program}}:
{func} setup() {{
{body}
}}

H1108:
the first value of {name|q} at the top level of {file, select, testfile {a test file} other {a module}} is not a constant expression: {part|q} is not constant (loading {file, select, testfile {a test file} other {a module}} runs no code, 1.1). Build the value in a function; each function or test that uses it calls {fn}() once and keeps the result in a variable:
{func} {fn}(){type, select, empty {} other { -> {type}}} {{
    {return} {value}
}}

H1114:
the first value of {name|q} at the top level of {file, select, testfile {a test file} other {a module}} is not a constant expression: {part|q} is not constant (loading {file, select, testfile {a test file} other {a module}} runs no code, 1.1). Functions assign to {name|q}, so it is shared state: start it as none; each function or test that uses it calls setup_{name}() first, and the first call builds the value once:
{var} {name}: {type, select, empty {<type>} other {{type}}}? = {none}
{func} setup_{name}() {{
    {if} {name} == {none} {{
        {name} = {value}
    }}
}}
